q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 770.3661 cm .086275 .196078 .309804 rg BT/F2 11.5 Tf 0 3 TD (C.11.1 The collapse itself, drawn)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 709.3661 cm 0 0 0 rg BT .845433 Tw/F1 10 Tf 0 46 TD (Three of this appendix's findings turn on a single phenomenon, so it is worth isolating. GPT-2's mean-pooled)Tj .808259 Tw 0 -14 TD (caption vectors have an effective rank of 6.5 out of 768 and a mean pairwise cosine of +0.999: one direction)Tj .005346 Tw T* (carries 59.6 )Tj[-3613.535]TJ ( of all variance, and every caption sits in a cone a couple of degrees wide. Cosine between)Tj 0 Tw T* (any two of them reads near 1.000 regardless of what they say.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 633.3661 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 1.640433 Tw/F1 10 Tf 0 60 TD (The origin is the training objective. GPT-2 optimises next-token prediction and nothing else; it has no CLS)Tj -.126063 Tw 0 -14 TD (token, because its attention is causal and a prepended summary token would see nothing, no pooling layer, and)Tj 2.530433 Tw T* (no similarity loss. It never produced a sentence-level vector during training - that vector is this project's)Tj 2.369183 Tw T* (construction, a mean over token states optimised for a different task - and averaging surfaces the large)Tj 0 Tw T* (component every passage shares.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 557.3661 cm 0 0 0 rg BT -.062067 Tw/F1 10 Tf 0 60 TD (The consequences are the three results already reported. The fitted map scores cosine 1.000 while retrieving at)Tj .171417 Tw 0 -14 TD (R@1 0.160, with held-out R-squared 0.414: the content IS predicted, at 71 )Tj[-3630.142]TJ ( of the bge arm, and cosine)Tj .153718 Tw T* (simply cannot read it. A label-free linear transform corrects it, raising effective rank to 490.8 and R@1 to 0.478.)Tj 1.773937 Tw T* (And it forms the bottom rung of the pre-registered ladder in Section C.14, where raw retrieval across four)Tj 0 Tw T* (training objectives ordered by effective rank with rank correlation +1.00.)Tj ET Q q 481.8898 0 0 276.378 56.69291 269.3189 cm /Im1 Do Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 246.3189 cm 0 .023529 .4 rg BT/F1 8.6 Tf 8.007565 14.4 TD (Figure C5b: the collapse and its spectrum, the metric disagreement it causes, its origin, the label-free fix, and what it does not)Tj 79.11139 -11.5 TD (destroy. The point cloud in panel A is schematic; every number shown is measured.)Tj ET Q q 0 0 0 rg 0 0 0 RG BT/Helvetica 10 Tf 107.777698 727.39889 TD[(percent)]TJ ET Q
